From 2bfd294a87e79d7e5ff2a74c9c11d70750ec2136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Dompet naming bug, add Tutup Dompet, build Arus Kas +
 wire to Dompet
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Bug fix: cash_movements.type / kasbon.status naming mismatch
   DompetRepository wrote CashMovementType.cashSale.name ("cashSale")
   and KasbonStatus.partiallyPaid.name ("partiallyPaid") — camelCase —
   while the DB schema and seed data use snake_case ("cash_sale",
   "partially_paid"). The parser's exact-match firstWhere() silently
   fell back to `adjustment` on any mismatch, so every real cash sale
   showed up in the UI as a generic "Penyesuaian" instead of "Penjualan
   Cash". Added explicit dbValue/fromDbValue to both enums and updated
   every read/write site to use them instead of .name.

2. Tutup Dompet (closing), built to the real PRD shape
   New dompet_closings table, DompetClosing/DompetClosingPreview
   models, and repository logic: Expected Cash = Opening + Cash Sales +
   Courier Deposits - Cash Expenses, closing blocked while any courier
   holds outstanding cash, discrepancy recorded as its own adjustment
   movement (ledger stays immutable). No Shift module exists yet, so a
   closing's period is "since the previous closing" rather than tied to
   a shift_id — documented in DompetClosing's doc comment for when
   Shift lands. New DompetClosingScreen wired to a header action on
   Dompet.

3. Arus Kas — real Flutter screen, wired into the Dompet ledger
   Was previously only an HTML preview; CashMovementType.expense was
   defined but never written anywhere, and Laporan was already querying
   cash_movements for type='expense' with no data to find. New
   cash_expenses table + ArusKasRepository: cash-location-funded
   entries write a matching cash_movement (recordCashExpense /
   recordCashIncome) so Dompet balances and Arus Kas totals stay
   traceable to each other; Non-Tunai entries skip this. Screen follows
   the Menu Management reference pattern (dropdown title switch, date
   filter row, floating add-form). Wired into the "Kas" grid tile.

Also fixed one regression introduced while touching KasbonStatus
(getKasbonList's status filter still used .name) and removed a dead
_sumberDanaInitialized flag that was never read.

Note: could not run flutter analyze/test in this environment (no
Flutter SDK, restricted network) — verified manually instead: brace/
paren balance on every touched file, every API call's signature
against its actual declaration, and Flutter-version compatibility
(DropdownButtonFormField.value over the newer initialValue, since
SETUP.md pins this project to Flutter 3.27+). Please run `flutter
analyze` on your end before merging.
